    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1005">

                <pb facs="1125" n="1029" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1029"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Lee to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-16T12:30:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">February 16,
                                1898—12.30 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> blown up and destroyed to-night at 9.40 p.m.
                    Explosion occurred well forward under quarters of crew; consequence many were
                    lost. It is believed all officers saved, but Jenkins and Merritt not yet
                    accounted for. Cause of explosion yet to be investigated. Captain-General and
                    Spanish army and navy officers have rendered every assistance. Sigsbee and most
                    of his officers on Ward steamer <hi rendition="#italic">City of Washington</hi>.
                    Others on Spanish man-of-war and in city. Am with Sigsbee now, who has
                    telegraphed Navy Department.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
